> But that's cheating a bit, since we are singularizing rather than using
> plural quantification. Maybe plural quantifier "su'oi ci" could be
> defined as:
>
>   su'oi ci broda cu brode := su'oi da poi broda zo'u ci de poi broda
> gi'e me da zo'u da brode
>
> Then we can say "su'oi ci tadni cu sruri lo dinju".

If {su'oi} is to parallel {su'o}, then I would expect {su'oi ci} to mean 
"at least three" as a plural quantifier.

But maybe {su'oi je ci} "at least one and three" makes sense for the 
exact plural 3. It's a bit hackish though, because it connects a plural 
with a singular quantifier.

Another option is to have a new PA that marks a PA string as plural.

And yet another option is to take plurals as the default.

